--- MESSAGE ---
An actor's reference parameter is a consumer of its message type, and sending is application

The six actor-minting parameters typed by the host's `ActorRef(M)` are `(M -> Unit)`, drake's own arrow,
and a send is `consumer(report)`. The assembly keeps the host's refs and converts each once at its
boundary when it hands a member its arguments; a member only applies a function, which Haskell realizes
as a function into IO and Scala as a Pekko ref wrapped in one. The four OriginateReport actions read the
consumer back from the session as a function, so the last Pekko leaves leave the corpus. The term
"ActorRef" is provisional until Pekko is integrated through drake definitions with implementations in
the Scala target. No engine change.

